+<h1>How to Convert PDF to Excel Free — No Upload, No Account</h1>
+<p>Stuck with a PDF full of tables you need to edit in a spreadsheet? You can extract tables directly from a PDF and get an editable Excel or CSV file — without uploading your document anywhere.</p>
+
+<div class="cta-box"><p>Convert PDF to Excel free — no upload, no account</p><a href="https://rightpdfkit.com/#pdf-to-excel" class="cta-btn">PDF to Excel Free →</a></div>
+
+<h2>How to convert PDF to Excel — step by step</h2>
+<ol>
+  <li>Open the <strong>PDF to Excel</strong> tool on RightPDFKit.</li>
+  <li>Upload your PDF — drag it in or click to browse.</li>
+  <li>The tool detects tables automatically. Preview the extracted data before downloading.</li>
+  <li>Choose your output format: <strong>.xlsx</strong> for Excel, or <strong>.csv</strong> for Google Sheets or any other tool.</li>
+  <li>Click <strong>Download</strong>.</li>
+</ol>
+
+<h2>What types of PDF tables convert well?</h2>
+<table>
+  <tr><th>PDF type</th><th>Conversion quality</th></tr>
+  <tr><td>Born-digital PDF (exported from Word, Excel, accounting software)</td><td class="good">✓ Excellent</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>PDF with simple, clean grid tables</td><td class="good">✓ Very good</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>PDF with merged cells or complex headers</td><td style="color:#e67e22;font-weight:700">◎ Good, may need minor cleanup</td></tr>
+  <tr><td>Scanned PDF (image of a document)</td><td class="bad">✗ Needs OCR first</td></tr>
+</table>
+<p>For scanned PDFs, use the <a href="ocr-extract-text-scanned-pdf.html">OCR tool</a> first to make the text selectable, then convert to Excel.</p>
+
+<h2>PDF to Excel vs copying and pasting</h2>
+<p>Manually copying tables from a PDF into Excel is tedious and error-prone — especially for multi-page tables or documents with dozens of rows. The converter extracts all tables at once, preserving row and column structure, so you don't have to reformat anything.</p>
+
+<h2>Common use cases</h2>
+<ul>
+  <li><strong>Financial statements and bank statements</strong> — import figures directly into your spreadsheet model</li>
+  <li><strong>Invoices and purchase orders</strong> — extract line items for reconciliation</li>
+  <li><strong>Research data and reports</strong> — pull tables into Excel for further analysis</li>
+  <li><strong>Government data PDFs</strong> — census tables, budget documents, statistical releases</li>
+</ul>
+
+<h2>Why convert without uploading?</h2>
+<p>Financial documents contain sensitive data — account numbers, transaction history, personal details. Tools that upload your PDF to a server expose that data unnecessarily. RightPDFKit converts entirely in your browser using client-side JavaScript. Nothing is ever sent to a server.</p>
